( Grbl-R4 demo program - Arduino UNO R4 WiFi / Renesas RA4M1 )
( )
( Envelope: X 0..98  Y 0..98  Z 0..5 mm, relative to wherever the )
( machine is standing when the program starts. Nothing ever goes )
( below Z0, so with the tool clear of the work this is a dry run. )
( )
( Before starting: jog to the front-left of the area you want used, )
( then zero X, Y and Z in UGS. The G10 L20 below zeroes them again )
( in case you did not - it does NOT need homing. It sets the G54 )
( offset, which survives a stop/reset; a G92 would not, and the )
( shown position would jump back when the program is stopped. )
( )
( Exercises: G0/G1, G2/G3 arcs and full circles, helical arcs, )
( G17/G18/G19 planes, G90/G91, G4 dwell, feed changes, and a long )
( fine-segment raster that keeps the planner and the link busy. )
( Path length about 2848 mm; expect roughly 2-6 minutes at the feeds )
( below, clamped by your $110-$112 max rates. 2656 lines. )

G21 (mm)
G90 (absolute)
G17 (XY plane)
G94 (units per minute)
G54 (work coordinate system 1)
G0Z5

( Spindle and coolant are left commented out on purpose: this file )
( does not know what you have wired to those outputs. Uncomment if )
( you want to exercise the PWM output on D11 and the relays. )
(M3 S1000)
(M8)
G4P0.5 (dwell half a second)

